body:
The distributed `agent-builder` agent template `opencode-suite/agents/agent-builder.md` (product source embedded into the `apg` binary via `include_str!` and installed by `apg init` into `~/.opencode/agents/`) must offer and generate only the agent roster the suite actually supports. The optional `coordinator` is dead weight — a `mode: primary` agent named in the template's roster that is never generated here — so every mention must be removed:
- the frontmatter `description:` (line 2) drops ", and an optional coordinator";
- the roster intro (lines 55-65) drops "and an optional `coordinator`", so the generated set is implementers only — the core/root `implementer`, per-subsystem `<name>-implementer`s, and tiered `test-implementer`s where a test tier is file-separable;
- the `### coordinator (optional)` section (lines 274-276) is deleted entirely;
- workflow step 3's interview bullet "Whether a `coordinator` is wanted." (line 379) is deleted;
- workflow step 4 (lines 381-383) no longer names an "optional `coordinator`" in the default plan;
- workflow step 5's scaffold line (line 385) becomes `mode: subagent` unconditionally — the "(optional `coordinator`: primary)" branch is removed;
- non-negotiable rule 8 (line 335) drops "and coordinator" from its example of generated names that need explicit navigator-allowlist entries.

IMPORTANT: the `coordinator` targeted here is the OPTIONAL GENERATED PRIMARY AGENT, not the coordinator ROLE the codebase-navigator performs in the feedback-routing / task-cadence prose. Every use of the word "coordinator" for that role is retained unchanged.

Acceptance criteria:
- `opencode-suite/agents/agent-builder.md` contains no offer or generation of an optional `coordinator` agent: no `### coordinator (optional)` section, no "whether a coordinator is wanted" interview bullet, no primary-mode scaffold branch, and no coordinator example in rule 8.
- Every generated agent is scaffolded `mode: subagent`.
- Scope is the one product-source file; the repo's own `.opencode/agents/**` are consumer artifacts and are NOT edited. No binary change.
- The rest of the template (permission-shape rules, gate rules, the register/verify steps) is otherwise unchanged by THIS requirement.
